column14:
No, it is not possible to implement an AVL tree with the described operation in \(O(1)\) time without affecting the runtime of the other operations.

 ```latex
 \text{Let's assume we have an AVL tree with the described operation.}
 \text{Let n be the number of nodes in the AVL tree.}

 \text{To return the minimal element that is greater than or equal to the average of the elements in } O(1) \text{ time, we need to keep track of the following:}
 \text{1. The average of the elements in the AVL tree.}
 \text{2. The minimal element that is greater than or equal to the average.}

 \text{Updating these values whenever there is an insert or delete operation in the AVL tree will take at least } O(\log n) \text{ time.}
 \text{Hence, it is not possible to implement the described operation in } O(1) \text{ time without affecting the runtime of the other operations.}
 ```

